# 7. PERMISSION MANAGEMENT

Develop a centralized permission engine.

Permission granularity must support:

**Module → Submodule → Feature → Action → Data Scope.**

Examples:

| Module | Feature | Action |
|---|---|---|
| Procurement | Purchase Requisition | View |
| Procurement | Purchase Requisition | Create |
| Procurement | Purchase Requisition | Edit |
| Procurement | Purchase Requisition | Submit |
| Procurement | Purchase Requisition | Approve |
| Procurement | Purchase Requisition | Reject |
| Procurement | Purchase Requisition | Cancel |
| Procurement | Purchase Requisition | Export |
| Finance | General Ledger | View |
| Finance | Journal Entry | Create |
| Finance | Journal Entry | Post |
| Finance | Accounting Period | Close |
| User Administration | User Master | Create |
| User Administration | Role Management | Assign Permissions |

Support permission types:

- View.
- Create.
- Edit.
