# 13. SEGREGATION OF DUTIES – SOD

Implement configurable segregation-of-duties rules.

Examples:

- User cannot approve their own PR where maker-checker is mandatory.
- User cannot create and approve the same supplier bank change.
- User cannot create and approve the same payment where segregation is required.
- User cannot change their own administrative role.
- User cannot approve their own permission elevation.

Support:

- Preventive controls.
- Warning controls.
- Authorized exception approvals.
- Conflict detection.
- Risk classification.
- Exception history.

Provide a role-conflict matrix and user-level conflict report.

Do not automatically label a conflict as fraud.

