# 29. ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA

The module is accepted only when:

1. Administrators can create and manage users.
2. Administrators can create and manage roles.
3. Permissions can be assigned at module, feature and action level.
4. Company and branch access is correctly restricted.
5. Purchase Organization access is correctly enforced.
6. Multiple role assignments work correctly.
7. Backend authorization is enforced.
8. Unauthorized API calls are rejected.
9. Access requests follow approved workflows.
10. Temporary access expires automatically.
11. Segregation-of-duties rules are enforced.
12. Existing authentication and Email 2FA continue working.
13. Login and security activities are audited.
14. New modules and features are registered in the permission registry.
15. New permissions are not automatically granted.
16. Role impact is reported before permission grants.
17. Existing modules use the centralized authorization service.
18. Security and regression tests pass.
19. Documentation and project memory are updated.
